/-!
# The special fibre of a flat scheme over a discrete valuation ring is a principal divisor

Let `R` be a discrete valuation ring with uniformizer `π` and let `V` be an integral scheme,
locally of finite type and flat over `Spec R`, of delta-dimension `n` for the base situation
`Stacks.Chow.dvrChowSituation R`. The special fibre `V_κ ⊆ V` — the scheme-theoretic fibre of
`V ⟶ Spec R` over the closed point — is cut out, on every affine open `U ⊆ V`, by the single
function that `π` determines there, and flatness makes that function a nonzerodivisor. So `π`,
read as a rational function on `V`, is a global equation for the special fibre, and the
`(n-1)`-cycle of the special fibre is the principal divisor of that rational function:

  `[V_κ]_{n-1} = div(π)`.

Both sides are compared coefficientwise. At a point of codimension other than one both vanish:
the order of vanishing of any rational function does by Stacks 02RO, and the cycle of a closed
subscheme does because a point of delta-dimension `n - 1` on an integral scheme of
delta-dimension `n` is exactly a point of codimension one, which is Stacks 02RK. At a point of
codimension one inside the special fibre the two coefficients agree because the local equation
of the special fibre there is the germ of `π`, which is the multiplicity comparison of Stacks
02QU; and at a point of codimension one outside the special fibre both vanish again, because
there `π` generates the unit ideal of the local ring.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.dvrUniformizerFunctionField` — a uniformizer of the base, read as a rational
  function on the total space.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.ker_fiberι_closedPoint` — the sheaf of ideals of the scheme-theoretic fibre over
  the closed point is the one cut out by the residue field of the maximal ideal.
* `Stacks.Chow.ker_fiberι_ideal_eq_span` — **the local equation of the special fibre**: on every
  affine open its ideal is generated by the function a uniformizer cuts out there.
* `Stacks.Chow.dvrUniformizerFunctionField_ne_zero` — a uniformizer is nonzero as a rational
  function on a scheme flat over the base.
* `Stacks.Chow.cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_fiberι_ker_eq_principalDivisorCycle` — **the
  special fibre is the principal divisor of a uniformizer.**

## Implementation notes

The special fibre appears here as `(sV.fiberι (IsLocalRing.closedPoint R)).ker`, the kernel
ideal sheaf of the projection from `V ×_{Spec R} Spec κ(s)`, whereas the local equation of
`Stacks.Models.specialFiberIdeal_ideal_eq_span` is stated for `Spec` of an abstract residue
field. The two are identified in `Stacks.Chow.ker_pullback_fst_fromSpecResidueField`: over the
spectrum of a local ring the canonical morphism from the spectrum of the residue field at the
closed point factors as an isomorphism followed by `Spec` of the residue map, and a kernel ideal
sheaf is unchanged by precomposition with an isomorphism.

`Stacks.Chow.dvrUniformizerFunctionField` is defined through the global sections, since
`Stacks.Models.chartHom` is available on every open and the germ at the generic point does not
depend on which open the function is read on; `Stacks.Chow.germToFunctionField_chartHom`
records that independence and is what connects the global definition to the affine opens on
which the local equation is available.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02RO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02RO)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C5Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C5Z)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.Chow

/-! ### The scheme-theoretic fibre over the closed point -/

/-- The kernel ideal sheaf of the projection from the fibre over a point of an affine base is
the inverse image of the kernel ideal sheaf of `Spec` of the residue map, whenever the canonical
morphism from the spectrum of the residue field factors as an isomorphism followed by that
`Spec`: a kernel ideal sheaf does not change under precomposition with an isomorphism. -/
theorem ker_pullback_fst_fromSpecResidueField {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) (x : ↥(Spec (.of R))) {κ : Type u} [CommRing κ] [Algebra R κ]
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (algebraMap R κ))
    (e : (Spec (.of R)).residueField x ≅ CommRingCat.of κ)
    (he : Spec.map e.inv ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R κ)) =
      (Spec (.of R)).fromSpecResidueField x) :
    (pullback.fst f ((Spec (.of R)).fromSpecResidueField x)).ker =
      (pullback.fst f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R κ)))).ker := by
  have : IsClosedImmersion (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R κ))) :=
    IsClosedImmersion.spec_of_surjective _ hsurj
  have he2 : Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R κ) ≫ e.inv) =
      (Spec (.of R)).fromSpecResidueField x := by
    rw [Spec.map_comp]; exact he
  have : IsClosedImmersion ((Spec (.of R)).fromSpecResidueField x) := by
    rw [← he2]
    refine IsClosedImmersion.spec_of_surjective _ ?_
    exact (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso e.inv).2.comp hsurj
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_fst_of_isClosedImmersion,
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_fst_of_isClosedImmersion, ← he,
    Scheme.Hom.ker_comp_of_isIso]

/-- **The special fibre as a kernel ideal sheaf.** The scheme-theoretic fibre of a scheme over a
local ring taken over the closed point is cut out by the same sheaf of ideals as the base change
along `Spec` of the quotient map to the residue field of the maximal ideal. -/
theorem ker_fiberι_closedPoint {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) :
    (f.fiberι (IsLocalRing.closedPoint R)).ker =
      (pullback.fst f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
        (algebraMap R (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R).ResidueField)))).ker :=
  ker_pullback_fst_fromSpecResidueField f (IsLocalRing.closedPoint R)
    (Ideal.algebraMap_residueField_surjective (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R))
    (Scheme.Spec.residueFieldIso (CommRingCat.of R) (IsLocalRing.closedPoint R))
    (Scheme.Spec.map_residueFieldIso_inv_eq_fromSpecResidueField _ _)

/-- The residue field of a local ring, in the sense of `IsLocalRing.ResidueField`, and the
residue field of its maximal ideal, in the sense of `Ideal.ResidueField`, agree as
`R`-algebras: the quotient by a maximal ideal is already a field, so localizing it changes
nothing. -/
def dvrResidueFieldAlgEquiv (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] :
    IsLocalRing.ResidueField R ≃ₐ[R] (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R).ResidueField :=
  AlgEquiv.ofBijective
    (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom R (R ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R)
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R).ResidueField)
    (Ideal.bijective_algebraMap_quotient_residueField _)

/-! ### Functions coming from the base ring -/

/-- The morphism from the spectrum of the sections on an affine open to the base is `Spec` of
the ring map through which those sections are an algebra over the base ring. -/
theorem fromSpec_comp_eq_SpecMap_chartHom {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    hU.fromSpec ≫ f = Spec.map (Stacks.Models.chartHom f U) := by
  dsimp only [Stacks.Models.chartHom]
  rw [Spec.map_comp]
  simpa [Scheme.isoSpec_Spec_inv, IsAffineOpen.fromSpec_top] using
    (IsAffineOpen.SpecMap_appLE_fromSpec f (isAffineOpen_top (Spec (.of R))) hU (by simp)).symm

/-- A nonzerodivisor of the base ring cuts out a nonzero function on every nonempty affine open
of an integral scheme flat over that base: flatness keeps it a nonzerodivisor on the sections,
and a nonzerodivisor of a domain is nonzero. -/
theorem chartHom_apply_ne_zero {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X]
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [Flat f] {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    [Nonempty U] {π : R} (hπ : π ∈ nonZeroDivisors R) :
    (Stacks.Models.chartHom f U).hom π ≠ 0 := by
  let : Algebra R Γ(X, U) := (Stacks.Models.chartHom f U).hom.toAlgebra
  have : IsDomain Γ(X, U) := IsIntegral.component_integral U
  have hnzd : algebraMap R Γ(X, U) π ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, U) :=
    Stacks.Models.map_mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_flat π hπ f hU.fromSpec
      (fromSpec_comp_eq_SpecMap_chartHom f hU)
  exact mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_ne_zero.mp hnzd

/-- **The local equation of the special fibre.** On every affine open of a scheme flat over a
discrete valuation ring, the ideal of the scheme-theoretic fibre over the closed point is
generated by the function a uniformizer cuts out there. -/
@[sga "6 X 7.8" "partial", sga "7 X 1.8" "partial"]
theorem ker_fiberι_ideal_eq_span {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing R] {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [Flat f]
    {π : R} (hπ : Irreducible π) (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    (f.fiberι (IsLocalRing.closedPoint R)).ker.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩ =
      Ideal.span {(Stacks.Models.chartHom f U).hom π} := by
  rw [ker_fiberι_closedPoint f]
  exact Stacks.Models.specialFiberIdeal_ideal_eq_span (dvrResidueFieldAlgEquiv R) f hπ U hU

/-! ### A uniformizer as a rational function -/

/-- **A uniformizer, read as a rational function on the total space**: the germ at the generic
point of the global function that the uniformizer cuts out. -/
def dvrUniformizerFunctionField {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing R] {V : Scheme.{u}} (sV : V ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [IsIntegral V]
    (π : R) : V.functionField :=
  haveI : Nonempty (⊤ : V.Opens) := ⟨⟨Classical.arbitrary V, trivial⟩⟩
  (V.germToFunctionField (⊤ : V.Opens)).hom ((Stacks.Models.chartHom sV (⊤ : V.Opens)).hom π)

/-- The rational function a uniformizer determines is the one its global function determines. -/
theorem dvrUniformizerFunctionField_eq {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing R] {V : Scheme.{u}} (sV : V ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [IsIntegral V]
    (π : R) [Nonempty (⊤ : V.Opens)] :
    dvrUniformizerFunctionField sV π =
      (V.germToFunctionField (⊤ : V.Opens)).hom
        ((Stacks.Models.chartHom sV (⊤ : V.Opens)).hom π) :=
  rfl

/-- The rational function a uniformizer determines can be read on any nonempty open: the
functions it cuts out on the various opens restrict to one another, and germs at the generic
point are compatible with restriction. -/
theorem germToFunctionField_chartHom {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing R] {V : Scheme.{u}} (sV : V ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [IsIntegral V]
    (π : R) (U : V.Opens) [Nonempty U] :
    (V.germToFunctionField U).hom ((Stacks.Models.chartHom sV U).hom π) =
      dvrUniformizerFunctionField sV π := by
  have : Nonempty (⊤ : V.Opens) := ⟨⟨Classical.arbitrary V, trivial⟩⟩
  rw [dvrUniformizerFunctionField_eq]
  have hres := congrArg (fun ψ : CommRingCat.of R ⟶ Γ(V, U) ↦ ψ.hom π)
    (Stacks.Models.chartHom_comp_map sV (homOfLE (le_top : U ≤ ⊤)).op)
  rw [← hres]
  exact V.presheaf.germ_res_apply (homOfLE (le_top : U ≤ ⊤)) (genericPoint V) _ _

/-- A uniformizer cuts out a nonzero function on every nonempty affine open of an integral scheme
flat over a discrete valuation ring. -/
private theorem chartHom_apply_ne_zero_of_irreducible {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing R] {V : Scheme.{u}} (sV : V ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [IsIntegral V] [Flat sV]
    {π : R} (hπ : Irreducible π) {U : V.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) [Nonempty U] :
    (Stacks.Models.chartHom sV U).hom π ≠ 0 :=
  chartHom_apply_ne_zero sV hU (mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero hπ.ne_zero)

/-- Around every point there is an affine open on which a uniformizer is nonzero and generates
the stalk of the ideal of the special fibre. -/
private theorem exists_isAffineOpen_stalk_fiberι_ker_eq_span {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing R] {V : Scheme.{u}} (sV : V ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [IsIntegral V] [Flat sV]
    {π : R} (hπ : Irreducible π) (z : V) :
    ∃ (U : V.Opens) (_ : IsAffineOpen U) (hzU : z ∈ U),
      (Stacks.Models.chartHom sV U).hom π ≠ 0 ∧
        IdealSheafData.stalk (sV.fiberι (IsLocalRing.closedPoint R)).ker z =
          Ideal.span {(V.presheaf.germ U z hzU).hom ((Stacks.Models.chartHom sV U).hom π)} := by
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hzU, -⟩ := exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset (U := ⊤) (x := z) (by simp)
  have : Nonempty U := ⟨⟨z, hzU⟩⟩
  exact ⟨U, hU, hzU, chartHom_apply_ne_zero_of_irreducible sV hπ hU,
    IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_span_germ_of_ideal_eq_span (U := ⟨U, hU⟩) hzU
      (ker_fiberι_ideal_eq_span sV hπ U hU)⟩

/-- A uniformizer is nonzero as a rational function on an integral scheme flat over the base:
it is nonzero already as a function on any affine open, and sections of an integral scheme
inject into the function field. -/
theorem dvrUniformizerFunctionField_ne_zero {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing R] {V : Scheme.{u}} (sV : V ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [IsIntegral V]
    [Flat sV] {π : R} (hπ : Irreducible π) :
    dvrUniformizerFunctionField sV π ≠ 0 := by
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hxU, -⟩ :=
    exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset (U := ⊤) (x := Classical.arbitrary V) (by simp)
  have : Nonempty U := ⟨⟨_, hxU⟩⟩
  rw [← germToFunctionField_chartHom sV π U]
  exact fun h ↦ chartHom_apply_ne_zero_of_irreducible sV hπ hU
    (Scheme.germToFunctionField_injective V U (by simpa using h))

/-! ### The special fibre is the principal divisor of a uniformizer -/

/-- The generic point of an integral scheme flat over a discrete valuation ring does not lie on
the special fibre: there a uniformizer generates the unit ideal, because the local ring at the
generic point is the function field and the uniformizer is nonzero in it. -/
@[sga "3 X 5.14.0" "special case"]
theorem genericPoint_notMem_range_fiberι_ker {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing R] {V : Scheme.{u}} (sV : V ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [IsIntegral V]
    [Flat sV] {π : R} (hπ : Irreducible π) :
    genericPoint V ∉
      Set.range (sV.fiberι (IsLocalRing.closedPoint R)).ker.subschemeι.base := by
  intro hη
  have hsupp := (Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι
    (sV.fiberι (IsLocalRing.closedPoint R)).ker).subset hη
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hηU, -⟩ :=
    exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset (U := ⊤) (x := genericPoint V) (by simp)
  have : Nonempty U := ⟨⟨genericPoint V, hηU⟩⟩
  have hz := (Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_support_iff_of_mem (U := ⟨U, hU⟩) hηU).mp hsupp
  rw [ker_fiberι_ideal_eq_span sV hπ U hU, Scheme.mem_zeroLocus_iff] at hz
  refine hz _ (Ideal.subset_span rfl) ?_
  rw [Scheme.mem_basicOpen V _ (genericPoint V) hηU]
  refine isUnit_iff_ne_zero.mpr fun h ↦ ?_
  exact chartHom_apply_ne_zero_of_irreducible sV hπ hU
    (germ_injective_of_isIntegral V (genericPoint V) hηU (by simpa using h))

/-- Off the special fibre a uniformizer has order of vanishing zero: its germ generates the
whole local ring there, so the quotient by the ideal it generates is trivial. -/
theorem ord_dvrUniformizerFunctionField_eq_zero_of_notMem_range {R : Type u} [CommRing R]
    [IsDomain R] [IsDiscreteValuationRing R] {V : Scheme.{u}} (sV : V ⟶ Spec (.of R))
    [IsIntegral V] [IsLocallyNoetherian V] [Flat sV] {π : R} (hπ : Irreducible π) {z : V}
    (hco : Order.coheight z = 1)
    (hz : z ∉ Set.range (sV.fiberι (IsLocalRing.closedPoint R)).ker.subschemeι.base) :
    V.ord (dvrUniformizerFunctionField sV π) z = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨U, -, hzU, htne, hstalk⟩ := exists_isAffineOpen_stalk_fiberι_ker_eq_span sV hπ z
  have : Nonempty U := ⟨⟨z, hzU⟩⟩
  set t : Γ(V, U) := (Stacks.Models.chartHom sV U).hom π
  have htop : IdealSheafData.stalk (sV.fiberι (IsLocalRing.closedPoint R)).ker z = ⊤ := by
    refine (IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support _ z).mpr fun hmem ↦ hz ?_
    exact (Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι
      (sV.fiberι (IsLocalRing.closedPoint R)).ker).symm.subset hmem
  have hspan : Ideal.span {(V.presheaf.germ U z hzU).hom t} = ⊤ := hstalk ▸ htop
  have hord : Ring.ord ↑(V.presheaf.stalk z) ((V.presheaf.germ U z hzU).hom t) =
      ((0 : ℕ) : ℕ∞) := by
    have hdef : Module.length ↑(V.presheaf.stalk z)
        (↑(V.presheaf.stalk z) ⧸ Ideal.span {(V.presheaf.germ U z hzU).hom t}) =
        Ring.ord ↑(V.presheaf.stalk z) ((V.presheaf.germ U z hzU).hom t) := rfl
    rw [← hdef, hspan, Nat.cast_zero]
    exact Module.length_eq_zero_iff.mpr (Ideal.Quotient.subsingleton_iff.mpr rfl)
  rw [← germToFunctionField_chartHom sV π U]
  simpa using ord_eq_ringOrd_germ hco hzU t htne hord

/-- **The special fibre is the principal divisor of a uniformizer.** On an integral scheme `V`
of delta-dimension `n`, locally of finite type and flat over a discrete valuation ring `R`, the
`(n-1)`-cycle of the scheme-theoretic fibre over the closed point is the principal divisor of a
uniformizer of `R`, read as a rational function on `V`. -/
@[ega "IV 21.6.7" "special case", sga "7 X 1.8" "partial"]
theorem cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_fiberι_ker_eq_principalDivisorCycle
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsDiscreteValuationRing R] {V : Scheme.{u}}
    (sV : V ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [LocallyOfFiniteType sV] [IsIntegral V] [Flat sV]
    {n : ℤ} (hn : schemeDeltaDimension (dvrChowSituation R) sV = (n : EInt))
    {π : R} (hπ : Irreducible π) :
    cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme (dvrChowSituation R) sV
        ((sV.fiberι (IsLocalRing.closedPoint R)).ker).subschemeι (n - 1) =
      principalDivisorCycle (dvrChowSituation R) sV hn (dvrUniformizerFunctionField sV π) := by
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian V := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian sV
  have hgen := genericPoint_notMem_range_fiberι_ker sV hπ
  refine Subtype.ext (Function.locallyFinsuppWithin.ext fun z ↦ ?_)
  by_cases hco : Order.coheight z = 1
  · by_cases hzZ : z ∈ Set.range (sV.fiberι (IsLocalRing.closedPoint R)).ker.subschemeι.base
    · obtain ⟨U, -, hzU, htne, hstalk⟩ := exists_isAffineOpen_stalk_fiberι_ker_eq_span sV hπ z
      have : Nonempty U := ⟨⟨z, hzU⟩⟩
      have hkey := principalDivisorCycle_apply_eq_cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_apply
        (dvrChowSituation R) sV hn (sV.fiberι (IsLocalRing.closedPoint R)).ker hgen hco hzZ
        hzU ((Stacks.Models.chartHom sV U).hom π) htne hstalk
      rw [germToFunctionField_chartHom sV π U] at hkey
      exact hkey.symm
    · rw [cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_apply_eq_zero_of_notMem_range (dvrChowSituation R)
        sV _ (n - 1) hzZ, principalDivisorCycle_apply]
      exact (ord_dvrUniformizerFunctionField_eq_zero_of_notMem_range sV hπ hco hzZ).symm
  · rw [principalDivisorCycle_apply, V.ord_eq_zero_of_coheight_neq_one hco]
    refine cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_apply_eq_zero (dvrChowSituation R) sV _ (n - 1) z ?_
    rintro ⟨ξ, -, hdim⟩
    exact hco ((relativeDimension_eq_sub_one_iff_coheight_eq_one (dvrChowSituation R) sV hn z).mp
      hdim)

end Stacks.Chow

end
